[1920,1080]"><node index="0" text="" resource-id="" class="android.widget.ScrollView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="true" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,24][1890,1056]"><node index="0" text="“For roughly fifteen years”, his father confirmed. His face did the thing it did around certain objects – nothing at all, with tremendous force. “You kept a piece of Voldemort's soul in your headquarters. Next to the tea.”" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,24][1890,52]" /><node index="1" text="“A piece of his what?”, Harry asked." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,76][453,118]" /><node index="2" text="The kitchen took a moment to digest the phrase piece of Voldemort's soul. Tom saw comprehension travel from face to face like a slow curse. Dumbledore closed his eyes, briefly, an old man arriving at a conversation he had been postponing for years. His father gave him a look, which was how chores were assigned in their family." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,142][1890,268]" /><node index="3" text="“A Horcrux”, Tom began and enjoyed, in a small professional way, the flinch that went through a third of their hosts at the word alone. They seemed very prone to flinching at things. “Wizards and witches agree, nearly universally, that the soul is indivisible. Wizards and witches are wrong, as per usual. It can be divided. The instructions are short and simple: you commit a murder – a cold-blooded murder – and the recoil cracks the soul along the fault. Then you decant the loose piece into a vessel.”" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,292][1890,460]" /><node index="4" text="He nodded at the locket. “The piece anchors you. Destroy the body, and the rest of the person persists – discorporate, diminished, probably extremely annoyed – for as long as any anchor survives.”" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,484][1890,568]" /><node index="5" text="“That's why he didn't die”, Harry realized. “That night. The curse rebounded and he – that's why.”" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,592][1175,634]" /><node index="6" text="“That's why he didn't die properly”, Tom corrected him." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,658][679,700]" /><node index="7" text="“How do you know all of this?” It came from the scarred man with the magic eye." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,724][998,766]" /><node index="8" text="“He reads books,” his father supplied." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,790][477,832]" /><node index="9" text="Several of their hosts looked as though they had a few choice words about the sort of books his father apparently let Tom read, but none of them managed to voice them, because that’s when the old elf came up off the table like something exhumed – bat ears, bloodshot eyes, a filthy rag worn with more dignity than most men wore dress robes – with both gnarled hands clamped around the locket, braced for theft." resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,856][1890,982]" /><node index="10" text="“Thief! Thieves and blood traitors in Mistress's house and a stranger wanting it, wanting to take it, it is not his, it is not theirs—”" resource-id="" class="android.widget.TextView" package="com.fandomreader" content-desc="" checkable="false" checked="false" clickable="false" enabled="true" focusable="false" focused="false" scrollable="false" long-clickable="false" password="false" selected="false" bounds="[30,1006][1546,1048]" /></node></node></node></node></node></node></node></hierarchy>